A||||9||GT Bastard||Anybody race a Jetta VR6?||||2||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||10-11-2000||02:10 PM||||About a week or so ago I met this guy who drives an '86 SE, V6, automatic. He started coming to Perkins me and a couple other Fiero guys.  Anyhow, we're the first to get there and we're just standing around waiting for the others to show up.  Out of nowhere, the guy says "I know my automatic is slow, but my Jetta would waste any Fiero in a race."  I wasn't really interested in racing him, so I just said "yeah, you're prolly right."  So as we're sitting in Perkins, he starts spouting off about his Jetta GTI, VR6 with a 5sp and intake, exhaust, computer mods.  Another Friend of mine has been in his car before and agreed that he'd probably stomp me.  Then he starts saying that we should drop by his house and pick it up so that we can race(3am in the morning.)  I finally agreed, and we headed out to a 6 mile stretch of road near a small town.  Freshly paved, NO traffic.  His passenger counts to three, and I slipped the clutch at 1600rpm.  The pavement was cold, and I ended up spinning through most of 1st gear, but his Jetta was also doing a massive burnout(at least 30 foot!!!)  Then the guys stops and starts flashing his lights.  I pull up next to him again and he tells me that he missed second gear.  So anyhow, we raced AGAIN.  This time I got a better launch then before and easily pulled 4 car-lengths by the time I hit third.  This guy is laying down some serious rubber going into second AND third gear, but his car didn't seem all that quick.  Funny thing is, at about 80mph he started catching up.  At 100mph he passed me doing 130mph(according to him.)  We both shut down and he finally admitted that he underestimated the Fiero.  He still gave me the credit for the win since he didn't catch me till it was way too late.  We only planned on racing to 60mph(as we normally do) but the road was so perfectly smooth that we kept going.  Also, on the second launch the coolant temp plug fell off and my temp guage died(wierd...)  Fixed it of course, but it was really bizzarre...  So anyhow, those VR6's are pretty impressive top-end.  Thankyou, and goodbye.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   ||||reg||2
